win32u: a font-link chain that ends in nothing is not a chain.

`update_font_system_link_info` writes 32 SystemLink values from a hardcoded
table, and every entry in every one of them names a Microsoft CJK face --
MINGLIU.TTC, SIMSUN.TTC, BATANG.TTC, MSGOTHIC.TTC, SEGUISYM.TTF. Those are
correct on Windows. On an Android phone they are not present, cannot be shipped,
and never resolve. Measured in a container:

  chains: 33   with at least one resolvable font: 1   entirely dead: 32

The one that resolves is `Cascadia Mono`, which Vessel seeds itself and Wine
therefore does not overwrite. Everything else -- Tahoma, and so `MS Shell Dlg`,
and so every dialog and every Chromium window -- asks for a fallback glyph and is
told there is none, while Unifont sits installed in `windows\Fonts` reachable
from exactly one family.

**The registry is not where this can be fixed, and that was established the
expensive way.** Seeding all 32 values works, and then `update_codepage` reaches

    /* already set correctly, but, as a HACK, update font link
       info anyway, so that old Proton prefixes are fixed */
    update_font_system_link_info();

which rewrites all 32 from the table on *every* font init, changed or not. The
seeded values were watched reverting inside a single session, after `regedit` had
imported them and before the first window was drawn. A seed can only add names
Wine does not write; it can never keep one it does.

So the tail is appended here instead, to every value the function writes:

    NotoSansSymbols-Regular-Subsetted.ttf   symlinked from /system/fonts
    unifont-17.0.05.otf                     the BMP, 58,911 glyphs
    unifont_upper-17.0.05.otf               above the BMP, 59,057 glyphs

**Appended, and last.** `load_system_links` drops an entry whose file
`find_face_from_filename` cannot locate, with one TRACE, so this is inert on a
machine that has the real CJK fonts and is the only tier that answers on one that
does not. Last matters on its own: put Unifont anywhere earlier and it wins
glyphs a real typeface would have drawn better, which is the one way to make this
change look like a regression.

**Why the NUL arithmetic is what it is.** `len` counts the sequence's own
terminating NUL, so it is dropped before the tail is copied in. Appending without
dropping it would leave every tail entry sitting *after* the NUL that ends the
sequence, where `load_system_links` -- which walks until it meets an empty entry
-- would never read one of them: a change that writes the right bytes and links
nothing. Verified against a standalone harness before building: two original
entries plus three tail entries, walked the way `load_system_links` walks them,
double-NUL terminated.

Two fonts and not one because a TrueType glyph id is 16 bits: 58,911 + 59,057 is
117,968 glyphs against a ceiling of 65,535, so the BMP and everything above it
cannot share a file.

**These three filenames are also spelled in `native/pins.env` and asserted against
the staged payload by `build/tools.sh`.** A Unifont version bump changes the
filename, and a stale name here does not fail loudly -- it resolves to nothing and
the chain quietly ends where it began. That is this patch's maintenance cost and
it is written down rather than left to be found.

--- a/dlls/win32u/font.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/font.c
@@ -1672,6 +1672,38 @@
     "MSYH.TTC,Microsoft YaHei UI\0"
     "SEGUISYM.TTF,Segoe UI Symbol\0";
 
+/* Vessel: the tier that ends every chain, because on this device every chain
+ * Wine writes above ends in nothing.
+ *
+ * The lists above name MINGLIU.TTC, SIMSUN.TTC, BATANG.TTC, MSGOTHIC.TTC and
+ * SEGUISYM.TTF -- Microsoft CJK faces that are correct on Windows, are not
+ * present on an Android phone, cannot be shipped with one, and never resolve.
+ * Measured in a container: 33 SystemLink chains, 32 of them with zero resolvable
+ * entries. So every program that is not conhost asks for a fallback glyph and is
+ * told there is none, while the fonts that would have answered sit installed.
+ *
+ * This cannot be fixed from the registry, which is where it was tried first.
+ * `update_font_system_link_info` rewrites all of these values from the table
+ * above, and the HACK in `update_codepage` calls it on every font init even when
+ * nothing changed, so a seeded value is stamped back before the first window is
+ * drawn. Verified by seeding all 32 and watching them revert inside one session.
+ *
+ * Appended rather than substituted, and last rather than first: an entry whose
+ * file `find_face_from_filename` cannot locate is dropped with one TRACE, so this
+ * is inert on a machine that has the real fonts, and on one that does not it is
+ * the only tier that answers. Last matters -- put Unifont anywhere else and it
+ * wins glyphs a real typeface would have drawn better.
+ *
+ * **These three filenames are also spelled in `native/pins.env` and asserted
+ * against the staged payload by `build/tools.sh`.** A Unifont version bump
+ * changes the filename, and a stale name here does not fail loudly: it resolves
+ * to nothing and the chain quietly ends where it began. That is this patch's
+ * maintenance cost, written down rather than left to be discovered. */
+static const char vessel_system_link_tail[] =
+    "NotoSansSymbols-Regular-Subsetted.ttf\0"
+    "unifont-17.0.05.otf\0"
+    "unifont_upper-17.0.05.otf\0";
+
 static const char system_link_tahoma_non_cjk[] =
     "MSGOTHIC.TTC,MS UI Gothic\0"
     "MINGLIU.TTC,PMingLiU\0"
@@ -2992,6 +3024,32 @@
     free( valueW );
 }
 
+/* Vessel: [set_multi_value_key] with [vessel_system_link_tail] appended.
+ *
+ * `len` counts the sequence's own terminating NUL, so it is dropped before the
+ * tail is copied in -- otherwise the tail would sit after the NUL that ends the
+ * sequence, and `load_system_links`, which walks until it meets an empty entry,
+ * would never read one of them. On allocation failure this writes exactly what
+ * upstream would have: a chain without the tail is what this device has today
+ * and is strictly better than no chain at all. */
+static void vessel_set_multi_value_key( HKEY hkey, const WCHAR *name, const char *value, UINT len )
+{
+    UINT head = len ? len - 1 : 0;
+    char *joined;
+
+    if (!value || !(joined = malloc( head + sizeof(vessel_system_link_tail) )))
+    {
+        if (value) ERR( "malloc of %u failed, writing the chain without a fallback tier\n",
+                        (unsigned int)(head + sizeof(vessel_system_link_tail)) );
+        set_multi_value_key( hkey, name, value, len );
+        return;
+    }
+    memcpy( joined, value, head );
+    memcpy( joined + head, vessel_system_link_tail, sizeof(vessel_system_link_tail) );
+    set_multi_value_key( hkey, name, joined, head + sizeof(vessel_system_link_tail) );
+    free( joined );
+}
+
 static void update_font_system_link_info(void)
 {
     HKEY hkey;
@@ -3030,12 +3088,12 @@
                     break;
                 }
             }
-            set_multi_value_key(hkey, link_reg->font_name, link, len);
+            vessel_set_multi_value_key(hkey, link_reg->font_name, link, len);
         }
-        set_multi_value_key(hkey, arialW, link, len);
-        set_multi_value_key(hkey, arial_boldW, link, len);
-        set_multi_value_key(hkey, courier_newW, link, len);
-        set_multi_value_key(hkey, courier_new_boldW, link, len);
+        vessel_set_multi_value_key(hkey, arialW, link, len);
+        vessel_set_multi_value_key(hkey, arial_boldW, link, len);
+        vessel_set_multi_value_key(hkey, courier_newW, link, len);
+        vessel_set_multi_value_key(hkey, courier_new_boldW, link, len);
         NtClose( hkey );
     }
 }
